From: PlayThing builder <builder@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ART: use the ART low-4GB allocator on x86_64 hosts

Rosetta for Linux ignores MAP_32BIT. Host dex2oat then gets memory above
4 GiB, and it aborts in dchecked_integral_cast when it makes the boot
image. The ART allocator uses address hints, which Rosetta honors.
arm64 and macOS hosts already use this allocator.

---
 runtime/mem_map.h | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/runtime/mem_map.h b/runtime/mem_map.h
--- a/runtime/mem_map.h
+++ b/runtime/mem_map.h
@@ -28,7 +28,9 @@

 namespace art {

-#if defined(__LP64__) && (defined(__aarch64__) || defined(__mips__) || defined(__APPLE__))
+// PlayThing: x86_64 is in this list because Rosetta for Linux ignores MAP_32BIT.
+#if defined(__LP64__) && (defined(__aarch64__) || defined(__mips__) || defined(__APPLE__) || \
+    defined(__x86_64__))
 #define USE_ART_LOW_4G_ALLOCATOR 1
 #else
 #if defined(__LP64__) && !defined(__x86_64__)
